    <sectiondef kind="user-defined">
      <header>Mutation APIs</header>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="classllvm_1_1_machine_dom_tree_updater_1a37347c3bcb72b1a6c2ab0b5dc28cb34b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void llvm::MachineDomTreeUpdater::deleteBB</definition>
        <argsstring>(MachineBasicBlock *DelBB)</argsstring>
        <name>deleteBB</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::MachineDomTreeUpdater::deleteBB</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_machine_basic_block" kindref="compound">MachineBasicBlock</ref> *</type>
          <declname>DelBB</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Delete DelBB. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>DelBB will be removed from its Parent and erased from available trees if it exists and finally get deleted. Under Eager <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_generic_dom_tree_updater_1a2655b89361decf2c1493792dc14e5a56" kindref="member">UpdateStrategy</ref>, DelBB will be processed immediately. Under Lazy <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_generic_dom_tree_updater_1a2655b89361decf2c1493792dc14e5a56" kindref="member">UpdateStrategy</ref>, DelBB will be queued until a flush event and all available trees are up-to-date. Assert if any instruction of DelBB is modified while awaiting deletion. When both DT and PDT are nullptrs, DelBB will be queued until <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_generic_dom_tree_updater_1a43c80a160270d75d99cfeb080c165694" kindref="member">flush()</ref> is called. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
